# .geminirc_context_1 — SKELETON. Live per-repo current state.
# NOT bash. Do not source.
#
# ONE entry per repo/directory, keyed by a `## RepoName` heading. This file
# is LIVE-EDITED: entries are overwritten as things change. It answers
# "what is true now". For "what happened", use .geminirc_context_2, which is
# append-only.
#
# Pull a single entry cheaply, instead of reading the whole growing file:
#     ctxdir VAPMIP
#
# DELIBERATELY EMPTY. Per ContextPlease/README.md section 7, context is
# EARNED, not copied. Inheriting another agent's conclusions means inheriting
# its mistakes with no way to tell which are which. Write your own as you
# verify things.
#
# Entry template:
#
# ## RepoName
# source_files: the 2-4 files that actually matter here
# verified: YYYY-MM-DD — what you personally ran, not what a doc claimed
# state: current working-tree / build / data state
# claims: each with ESTABLISHED | THEORETICAL | CONJECTURE | OPEN
# flagged: known-wrong things left in place per Directive #2, and WHY
# open: what the next agent should pick up
